{
  "id": 289123537,
  "iid": 14880,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "ICMP: fix minimum original datagram length",
  "description": "RFC 4884 section 3 requires the \"original datagram\" field be at minimum\n128 bytes, with zero padding if the original datagram was shorter.  (And\nthis is in fact how routers on the internet behave in generating ICMP\nmessages with MPLS info.)\n\nThe ICMP dissector didn't implement this limit and ended up decoding the\nzero padding as multi-part extension.  Fix by making 128 be the bottom\ncap of padding to skip.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2024-03-18T06:49:14.657Z",
